      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the x-intercept of the parabola \\(x = 2y^2 - 6y + 3\\), we set \\(x = 0\\) and solve for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n0 = 2y^2 - 6y + 3.\n\\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in standard form:\n\\[\n2y^2 - 6y + 3 = 0.\n\\]\n\nWe use the quadratic formula, where \\(A = 2\\), \\(B = -6\\), and \\(C = 3\\):\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-B \\pm \\sqrt{B^2 - 4AC}}{2A}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate the discriminant:\n\\[\nB^2 - 4AC = (-6)^2 - 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 = 36 - 24 = 12.\n\\]\n\nNow, apply the quadratic formula:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-(-6) \\pm \\sqrt{12}}{2 \\cdot 2} = \\frac{6 \\pm \\sqrt{12}}{4}.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\sqrt{12} = 2\\sqrt{3}\\), we get:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the x-intercepts are:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nSo, the x-intercepts \\((a,0)\\), where \\(a = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) or \\(a = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\), will not contribute to a sum with the other intercepts.\n\nNext, compute the y-intercepts. Set \\(x = 0\\) and solve for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n0 = 2y^2 - 6y + 3.\n\\]\n\nThe y-intercepts can be found by setting \\(x = 0\\) and solving the quadratic equation \\(2y^2 - 6y + 3 = 0\\). As we have already solved for the x-intercepts, we can directly find the y-intercepts using the positive solutions of the quadratic equation which provide the y-intercepts:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\quad y = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the y-intercepts are \\((0, \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2})\\) and \\((0, \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2})\\).\n\nAdding the x-intercepts and y-intercepts:\n\\[\na = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\quad b = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\quad c = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum \\(a + b + c\\) is:\n\\[\na + b + c = \\left(\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right),\n\\]\n\nLet's simplify the expression:\n\\[\na + b + c = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3} + 3 + \\sqrt{3} + 3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{9}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{9}{2}}.\n\\]",
